{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBWindowMeasure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBWindowMeasure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBBorelCantelli","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.volume_window_le_geom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.volume_window_le_geom","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBWindowMeasure.lean#L81-L114","doc":"**Resonance-window measure bound (complete).**  For `1 < q` and `0 ≤ ε`,\n`volume(W(q,ε)) ≤ (1 − q^{−ε})·q/(q−1)` — the exact geometric bound.  Evaluates\n`volume_window_le`'s tsum: each term is `q^{−n}(1−q^{−ε}) = (q⁻¹)ⁿ(1−q^{−ε})`, a geometric\nseries summing to `(1−q^{−ε})·(1−q⁻¹)⁻¹ = (1−q^{−ε})·q/(q−1)`.  With\n`1 − q^{−ε} ≤ ε·log q`, this is `≤ ε·log q·q/(q−1)`, the summable resonance-window bound\nBorel–Cantelli consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.volume_window_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.volume_window_le","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBWindowMeasure.lean#L67-L79","doc":"**Measure reduction.**  `volume(W) ≤ Σ' n, (q^{−n} − q^{−(n+ε)})` — the window measure is\nbounded by the total length of the covering intervals (monotonicity + countable\nsubadditivity + `volume(Ioc a b) = b − a`).  The remaining geometric evaluation\n`Σ' n, q^{−n}(1−q^{−ε}) = (1−q^{−ε})·q/(q−1)` is bean `qou-a0li`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.window_subset_iUnion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.window_subset_iUnion","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBWindowMeasure.lean#L56-L65","doc":"**The resonance window is contained in a countable union of explicit intervals.**\n`W(q,ε) := {x ∈ (0,1) : s − ⌊s⌋ < ε} ⊆ ⋃ n, (q^{−(n+ε)}, q^{−n}]`.  This is the geometric\nheart of the measure estimate: each interval has length `q^{−n}(1−q^{−ε})`, summing to\n`(1−q^{−ε})·q/(q−1) ≤ ε·log q·q/(q−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.window_mem_Ioc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.window_mem_Ioc","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBWindowMeasure.lean#L33-L54","doc":"**Each window point lands in the explicit interval** `(q^{−(⌊s⌋+ε)}, q^{−⌊s⌋}]`.\nFrom `⌊s⌋ ≤ s < ⌊s⌋+ε` (the resonance condition) and `s·log q = log(1/x) = −log x`:\n`x ≤ q^{−⌊s⌋}` and `x > q^{−(⌊s⌋+ε)}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}